  "steps": [
    "In a large bowl, combine the chicken with the oil, yogurt, tomato paste, lemon juice, garlic, thyme or oregano, paprika, cinnamon, cumin, salt and pepper. Mix well, cover and marinate in the fridge 2-6 hours (overnight is best).",
    "Take the chicken out of the fridge 30 minutes before cooking. Heat the oven to 400°F and line a sheet pan with parchment.",
    "Spread the chicken on the pan without crowding and arrange the onion wedges around it. Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with the sumac.",
    "Roast 37-40 minutes, until the chicken is browned, reads at least 165°F, and the onions are soft.",
    "Meanwhile, make the sauce: stir together the yogurt, cucumber, dill, shallot, lemon juice, salt and pepper.",
    "Top the chicken with dollops of sauce, fresh herbs, diced cucumber, a dusting of sumac and a squeeze of lemon. Serve over rice, quinoa or in pita."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Swap in chicken breast for a leaner version, or add bell peppers or zucchini to the pan.",
    "Air fryer: 375°F for about 20 minutes, shaking halfway.",
    "Keeps 4 days in the fridge; store the sauce separately and reheat the chicken in the oven or on the stove."
  ],
